        "original_id": "cfb6139c-decb-551f-9e0e-46b75373144a",
        "text": "Page: Dale Hamer. Sentence: Dale Hamer is a former American football official in the National Football League (NFL) who served from 1978 to 2001, with a break taken for health reasons during the 1995 season.\nPage: Dale Hamer. Sentence: During his 23 seasons in the NFL, Hamer was assigned to officiate in two Super Bowls, as a head linesman in Super Bowl XVII and in Super Bowl XXII.\nPage: Super Bowl XVII. Sentence: Super Bowl XVII was an American football game between the American Football Conference (AFC) champion Miami Dolphins and the National Football Conference (NFC) champion Washington Redskins to decide the National Football League (NFL) champion for the 1982 season.",
